  "published": "2025-10-11T05:45:11.693Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- Some changes to make sure we can use expressions like this with \"&&\" and \"||\" operators:\n                \"MyObject.BooleanValue1 && Int1 == 15\" \"MyObject.BooleanValue1 || Int1 == 15\".\n                Before this change expressions similar to this would have to be used:\n                \"MyObject.BooleanValue1 == true && Int1 == 15\" && \"MyObject.BooleanValue1 == true || Int1 == 15\", since\n                Json path could not be used as an operand to \"&&\" and \"||\" unless it was an operand in some boolean operator or a\n                parameter in boolean function, that was itself an operand in \"&&\" or \"||\".\n            - Changes to make sure \"!\" evaluates to true for operands that evaluate to null or undefined.",
  "repository": "",
